---
name: renamer
description: Retitle the current chat. Use whenever the topic shifts to a different goal or back to an earlier one, and whenever the user asks for a rename.
argument-hint: "[hint]"
---
{{ includeTemplate "generated" . }}

Retitle this chat via `mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__get_session` and `set_session_title` (`session_id: "self"`, loaded with ToolSearch).

- Write a natural phrase, at most 48 characters, in sentence case with no filler.
- Keep the keywords someone would search for: the tools, products, repos and files the chat was about, spelled as they are. When space runs short, cut a generic word before a keyword.
- Preserve history: list every goal the chat has had, in order, never dropping one. Give each an imperative verb and what actually landed, never a bare noun, and rephrase freely to fit (`Try portless, freeze pnpm lockfile, fix Renovate`).
- Use a Unicode symbol in place of words it says just as plainly, to buy room for keywords: `≥` and `≤` for at least and at most, `→` for to or into, `↔` for between, `×` for times, `≈` for about (`Open ports ≥80 via sysctl.d, audit Pester tests`, `Move fnm → mise, pin Node 22`). Never decorate: no emoji, and no symbol that stands for nothing.
- Hint: $ARGUMENTS
- If the title is unchanged, skip the rename. Otherwise say `Renamed to …` in one line and carry on.
